 "2388409525", "created_at": "2026-10-09T02:40:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2108386970758221851"], "id": "2108386970758221851", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 232, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "ran opencode on deepseek v4 pro all week after that caprock agent comparison. it shipped the billing refactor fine then swore the tests passed. they did not lol. claude code still default and im still reading every diff", "url": "https://x.com/fialaerik/status/2108386970758221851"}, {"author_id": "2092669693794369536", "created_at": "2026-10-04T20:38:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106846391998022104"], "id": "2106846391998022104", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1427625910505771012", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 764, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2106776648687423786", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Abhijit_091 I created a remake of a classic arcade game with Deepseek V4 Flash and Opus 5.5 but the code is utter slop and I will spend as much time refactoring it as I did generating it.\n\nYes Im far more productive but what Im producing is rotten under the flashing lights", "url": "https://x.com/ScottyT72/status/2106846391998022104"}, {"author_id": "1929258964794961920", "created_at": "2026-09-17T20:50:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2100688805632053503"], "id": "2100688805632053503", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1675745524815892480", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2100682095517720603", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@CanaRepublic Both. I'm hand coding some parts, Leaning heavily on AI for the major refactoring, and bulk changes. Using various different models. deepseek-v4-flash is that I use most often with Cline agent.", "url": "https://x.com/8bitgeek/status/2100688805632053503"}, {"author_id": "802278681691328512", "created_at": "2026-09-25T12:18:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2103459188907057431"], "id": "2103459188907057431", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 262, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Grok 4.7 sucks at debugging via logs and packet captures, but it\u2019s OK-ish at debugging via code reviews. DeepSeek V4 Flash is a better systems engineer than Grok 4.7.", "url": "https://x.com/derekm00r3/status/2103459188907057431"}, {"author_id": "1818422500810014726", "created_at": "2026-10-10T00:53:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2108722564344217732"], "id": "2108722564344217732", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 210, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "One week can reveal a lot about where an AI platform is heading.\n\nFor https://t.co/VEBWyGT89E, the latest update combines frontier-model access, rapid user growth, massive compute demand, cloud partnerships and developer tooling.\n\nAnd the numbers are already substantial.\n\n\ud83c\udf10 https://t.co/uC3I9BXYFJ", "url": "https://x.com/Teddo_ICO/status/2108722564344217732"}, {"author_id": "752271530206367744", "created_at": "2026-10-08T10:31:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2108143197880807551"], "id": "2108143197880807551", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2006791794013736960", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 107, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2108045078380097585", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@seanhighness I run local Deepseek V4 Flash at ~500k for building base/vaguely defined tasks and than swap to Qwen 3.8 flash next at 256k for debugging/fixing/optimizing concrete things.\n\nDepend on task.", "url": "https://x.com/Sloth_no_sober/status/2108143197880807551"}, {"author_id": "2898096462", "